    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137-a9">

                <pb facs="0274" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg182"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gracey to Mr. Conger</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consular Service</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Fuchau, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-10-28"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copy
                    of a letter received by me from Rev. G. S. Miner, in reference to the
                    infringement of patent-right case, entered as No. 9 in this consulate. I think
                    Mr. Miner’s letter is self-explanatory and needs no further comment.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur T. Gracey</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul in Charge.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
